[38;2;248;248;242m            ues to concatenate include 1 for bold, 4 for underline, 5 for blink, 7 for inverse, 39 for default foreground color, 30 to[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            37  for  foreground  colors,  90  to 97 for 16-color mode foreground colors, 38;5;0 to 38;5;255 for 88-color and 256-color[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            modes foreground colors, 49 for default background color, 40 to 47 for background colors, 100 to  107  for  16-color  mode[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            background colors, and 48;5;0 to 48;5;255 for 88-color and 256-color modes background colors.[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m     LC_ALL, LC_COLLATE, LANG[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            These  variables specify the locale for the LC_COLLATE category, which determines the collating sequence used to interpret[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            range expressions like [a-z].[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m     LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, LANG[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            These variables specify the locale for the LC_CTYPE category, which determines the type of characters, e.g., which charac‐[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            ters are whitespace.  This category also determines the character encoding, that is, whether text  is  encoded  in  UTF-8,[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            ASCII,  or some other encoding.  In the C or POSIX locale, all characters are encoded as a single byte and every byte is a[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            valid character.[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m     LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            These variables specify the locale for the LC_MESSAGES category, which determines the language that  grep  uses  for  mes‐[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            sages.  The default C locale uses American English messages.[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m     POSIXLY_CORRECT[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            If set, grep behaves as POSIX requires; otherwise, grep behaves more like other GNU programs.  POSIX requires that options[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            that  follow  file  names must be treated as file names; by default, such options are permuted to the front of the operand[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            list and are treated as options.  Also, POSIX requires that unrecognized options be diagnosed as “illegal”, but since they[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m            are not really against the law the default is to diagnose them as “invalid”.[0m

